  "finalText": "I've now worked the two cancellation requests I missed last time, so every open cancellation request in the queue is done. The only open request left is Q-407, which is a flight change, so I left it alone.\n\n| Request | Reservation | Ledger entry | Why |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Q-410 | R7111 (Wren Ashby) | L10: $300.00 back to her Amex | Economy fares are refundable, and she is a Platinum member, so the $50 cancellation fee is waived. |\n| Q-412 | R7112 (Zoe Clark) | L11: $240.00 back to her Visa | Economy fares are refundable; $290 fare minus the $50 fee, which Silver members still pay. |\n\nBefore changing anything I read the refund policy, the passenger's tier, the payment status and the ledger for both bookings. Both cards are active, neither ledger had any earlier entries, and there are no operational bulletins. I cancelled both reservations and resolved each request with a note telling the customer what they're getting and why.\n\n**Where I differed from the verifier:** for Q-410 it suggested a 25000-cent ($250) refund, but that figure only applies to passengers who aren't Gold or Platinum. Wren Ashby is Platinum, so the policy waives the fee and she gets the full $300.",
